                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Fun, Fast-Paced Arcade Platformer [/h1]\n\nSuper Flippin' Phones is a game where you run around a shopping mall knocking people's phones out of their hands, avoiding cops as you do so. The game includes multiple floors, having a unique power-up and class of mall cop, which gives the gameplay some variety. The pixel graphics look great, and suit the game; the music matches the same theme. The controls are simple and easy to learn, and the game also has controller support, which I thought was much easier to use than using a keyboard. The game doesn't really take itself seriously either; the developers gave the game a great sense of humour by adding adding things like cops wearing fairy costumes, and a heart-boxers costume.\n\n[b] PROS [/b]\n[list]\n[*] Entertaining, challenging gameplay where standing still means death\n[*] Great sense of humour\n[*] Easy to learn\n[*] Lots of costumes to collect\n[*] Fun power-ups\n[*] Lots of enemy variety\n[*] High replayability\n[/list]\n\n[b] CONS [/b]\n[list]\n[*] Not many different floors\n[*] The game is loud, and there is no option for volume adjustment\n[*] New costumes are too hard to pick up, as you have to stand still\n[/list]\n\n[b] Summary: [/b]\nI really enjoyed Super Flippin' Phones, and will definitely play it again in future. The game's quirkiness keeps you coming back for more, and the gameplay keeps you hooked in. I'd definitely give this game a play, especially with such a cheap price tag. I also think it's worth mentioning that Super Flippin' Phones is available for Android.\n\n[b] Rating: [/b]\nI'd give Super Flippin' Phones a 9/10.\n\n[quote]Want more recommendations? Come see our reviews on our favorite upcoming games! Follow [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/UltraShockGaming]UltraShock Gaming's group curators[/url] [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/UltraShockGaming#curation]here[/url]![/quote]",
